# Claim 1

A method for inspecting a semiconductor wafer, comprising:

irradiating a surface of the semiconductor wafer with a laser beam along a single incident optical path so as to generate scattered light from the surface of the semiconductor wafer;

detecting a first portion of the scattered light through a first detection optical path having a first polarization characteristic and a first detection angle relative to the surface of the semiconductor wafer, thereby obtaining a first detection signal;

detecting a second portion of the scattered light through a second detection optical path having a second polarization characteristic different from the first polarization characteristic and a second detection angle different from the first detection angle, thereby obtaining a second detection signal;

detecting a third portion of the scattered light through a third detection optical path having a third polarization characteristic different from each of the first polarization characteristic and the second polarization characteristic and a third detection angle different from each of the first detection angle and the second detection angle, thereby obtaining a third detection signal; and

determining a presence, a size, and a type of a defect or a foreign matter present on the surface of the semiconductor wafer based on a comparison among the first detection signal, the second detection signal, and the third detection signal obtained simultaneously from the single irradiation of the laser beam.
